{
    "about": [
        "Headphone crossfeed: the Kotlin tests (CrossfeedTest) and the audio engine's Rust tests both check these.",
        "pole = exp(-2 pi cutHz / rate); feed = 10^(-feedDb / 20); gain = feed / (1 + feed) * (1 - pole).",
        "Per frame: d = gain * (R - L) + pole * d_prev (d starts at 0, kept in doubles); L' = L + d; R' = R - d.",
        "impulse: L = 1 at frame 0 and 0 after, R = 0 throughout; own is L' and other is R' (own[0] = 1 - gain, own[n] = -gain pole^n, other[n] = gain pole^n). Samples are 32-bit floats in and out.",
        "response: the size in dB of one side's sound in its own ear (1 - gain / (1 - pole e^-jw)) and in the other ear (gain / (1 - pole e^-jw)), w = 2 pi hz / rate.",
        "Presets: Natural 700 Hz 4.5 dB, Chu Moy 700 Hz 6 dB, Jan Meier 650 Hz 9.5 dB; Custom takes cutHz 300 to 2000 and feedDb 1 to 15."
    ],
    "tolerances": {
        "coefficient": 1.0E-12,
        "db": 1.0E-9,
        "floatSample": 1.0E-6
    },
